+## Summary
+
+Anyone can now see where every plan stands from the plan files alone, with no tracker reads and no model call:
+
+- `/list-plans` prints one line for each plan: its branch, Done against open, what is worked now, and the plans it waits on. `/list-plans --graph` draws each plan's branch against main, with its commits ahead and behind.
+- `/show-plan <id>` prints one plan as a tree. Not Started, In Progress, Now and Blocked are shown; Done and Dropped are hidden and counted; the plans it needs print after it. No status is worked out from the items under it (no roll-ups).
+- Every plan file now uses six statuses: Not Started, In Progress, Now, Done, Blocked, Dropped. `/shape-plan` writes Not Started for new items.
+- One template (`plan-view.md`) holds the marks and the layout of all three views; one plan tool prints them.
+
+The product model matches what was built. #806's thin page and spine entry are new, the pages of #628 and #729 are updated, and every change went through the model sub-agent and its skills. To make that possible, this change also carries the first piece of #979: the `link-model-part` skill (the spine entry of a domain, capability or feature, with its thin mark), the page skill reaching intent pages, and their route in `product-os-keeper`. Real names on six model pages became "the product owner".
+
+The agreed design: `.garura/project/issues/719/specs/design.md`.
+
+Closes #719, #729, #628, #806. Part of #979 (the shared play step comes later).
+
+## Fixed after the first review
+
+The first review (no blocking findings) found three defects, now fixed, each with its own test: the plan tool crashed on a plan with no title (it now stops with the file named); the file writer saved model files readable only by their owner (it now keeps a file's permissions — both copies, /shape-slice's too); and a write failing part way could leave the spine and the pages out of step (every written file is now put back).
+
+## Before it works for real
+
+- The template `plan-view.md` must be promoted to Phoenix memory; until then both plays stop at their first step with "template missing".
+- The install into this repo after the plan reaches main.
+
